      "span_id": "E1",
      "section_type": "results",
      "source_location": "3.2 Transverse-dominant anisotropic dispersion",
      "quoted_text": "For t > 0.5, the anisotropy stabilizes at a mean value of lambda approx 0.52 +/- 0.045. This result, lambda < 1, reveals a persistent and significant anisotropy where dispersion perpendicular to the local large-scale velocity systematically exceeds parallel dispersion."
    },
    {
      "span_id": "E2",
      "section_type": "results",
      "source_location": "3.3 Transient nature of vortex trapping",
      "quoted_text": "The function exhibits a rapid decay, crossing the 1/e threshold at a characteristic timescale of tau_Q approx 0.200."
    },
    {
      "span_id": "E3",
      "section_type": "results",
      "source_location": "3.3 Transient nature of vortex trapping",
      "quoted_text": "tracers remain trapped within a coherent vortex for only about 7-8% of a large-eddy turnover time. These trapping events are highly transient... insufficient to generate the long-term memory required for sustained superdiffusion."
    },
    {
      "span_id": "E4",
      "section_type": "results",
      "source_location": "3.4 Statistical properties of tracer displacements",
      "quoted_text": "By an intermediate time of t = 2.0, the displacement PDF is statistically indistinguishable from a Gaussian distribution... at late times (t = 5.0, 9.0), the PDFs... become platykurtic (light-tailed and flat-topped), with an excess kurtosis approaching -1.2."
    },
    {
      "span_id": "E5",
      "section_type": "results",
      "source_location": "3.5 Role of chaotic dynamics",
      "quoted_text": "the FTLE distributions for the Trapped and Free tracer cohorts are nearly identical... shows no relationship between a tracer's long-time FTLE and its residence fraction in vortices (Pearson r = 0.002)."
    },
    {
      "span_id": "E6",
      "section_type": "results",
      "source_location": "3.1 Temporal evolution of tracer dispersion",
      "quoted_text": "At early times (t < 0.3), transport is ballistic (alpha approx 2)... followed by a superdiffusive crossover... enters a diffusive regime (alpha approx 1) for 1.5 < t < 4... By the end of the simulation, 82.9% of tracers have crossed a periodic boundary, confirming that late-time statistics are dominated by these finite-domain effects."
    }
  ],
